      "title": "BORA: Bridging Offline Reinforcement Learning and Online Residual Adaptation for Real-World Dexterous VLA Models",
      "takeaway": "BORA targets real-robot adaptation of Vision-Language-Action (VLA) policies for dexterous manipulation, where high-DoF contact failures are hard to correct and online interaction is costly. It integrates an action-conditioned critic into a consistency-policy VLA, reuses that critic for frozen-base residual adaptation, and gathers corrective data via wearable arm-hand teleoperation plus a demonstration-guided local policy that converts coarse human intent into coordinated finger motions. Online rollouts and human corrections are mixed with offline data to update only a lightweight residual actor. On six real-world tasks across single-arm and bimanual platforms with two dexterous-hand models, 20 online trajectories per task raise average success from 60.8% to 82.5% on standard objects and 52% to 70% on held-out objects. Inspect how the residual actor is isolated and how intervention reliability is measured in bimanual twisting.",
